usion ensue  within the JSA guns posts have fans  curious about the director's intent  might there be a film-sized adaptation  of the 2020 strange adventures in the  cards even before Gunn became one of the  Architects of DC's media division he'd  shown an interest in the Publisher's  beloved Legacy titles in September 2022  Gunn tweeted that he'd been reading a  collection of strange Adventures what  seemed like a simple shot of his reading  material soon began to take on a deeper  significance on November 15th Gunn  posted an image of DC's Mr terrific AKA  Michael Holt a brilliant athletic  multi-millionaire who has given a new  purpose in life by joining the superhero  world after a string of private  tragedies to his Twitter the post  immediately sent Comics fans into a  tizzy and sparked debates about who  might play Mr terrific in a movie artist  Mitch Garretts replied the gun's tweet  saying what a strange Adventure this  could be the comic artist's comment came  alongside an image of a glowering Mr  terrific that immediately sparked  speculation that gun's post may be  leading into a big screen version of the  comic series Twitter hasn't been the  only place where gun has been busy he  set up a mastodon account on November  8th and immediately posted a photo of  the space-faring Bounty Hunter and  anti-hero Lobo it appears that gun is  fully dedicated to the unmined potential  of these characters who haven't appeared  in a big budget live-action movie yet I  have all sorts of ideas and we talk  about it all the time audiences will  have to wait and see if guns playful  teases lead anywhere but where there's  smoke there tends to be super powered  fire hopefully strange Adventures fans  will have a movie they can enjoy in due  time  laughs  [Music]
 

